 "source": "MikroElektronika Thermo K Click v102 (MIKROE-3311): the 3D zip (thermo_k_click_3d_file_v102.zip) has only a STEP (THERMO_K_click_v102.step, no DXF), so the outline and every part position come from the STEP assembly (the Board solid's corners; refdes products placed by their transforms), schematic v102. Outline: 25.4 x 38.71 mm with the 16.97 x 4.22 mm tab for the connector, one 2.54 mm chamfer at the bottom right. CN1 (PCC-SMP-K) drawn as its body's footprint from the STEP vertices (15.7 x 20.8 mm, socket face on the top edge), yellow for type K. ADDR SEL and PWR SEL are 0805 links at their STEP positions (ADDR on GND, 0x60; 3.3V), the schematic's. Header from the STEP at x 0/22.86, y 0-17.78 (standard). Estimated: silkscreen texts (none in the STEP; header labels from the schematic's nets), the MQFN drawn without its pads.",
